# Loaded alongside .env whenever NODE_ENV=test (Jest's default) — see
# @medusajs/utils's loadEnv. Only override what tests must never touch
# for real; everything else still comes from .env.
#
# Backstop, not the primary defense: order-placed and restock-subscribe
# both send real notifications via Resend as a side effect of actions
# integration tests take. Tests that reach those workflows should mock
# the `resend` module directly (see integration-tests/http/*.spec.ts) —
# that fully prevents the network call. This file only protects a test
# that forgets to: Resend still rejects the request, but with a real
# outbound call and an auth error instead of a silent real send.
RESEND_API_KEY=re_test_placeholder_not_a_real_key
RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=test@example.com
